## 🚧 Risk & Liability Management Page

Here's the complete Streamlit code snippet for your Risk & Liability Management analytics page:

```python
import streamlit as st
import pandas as pd

# Placeholder Data (replace with actual risk and liability data retrieval)
risk_liability_data = pd.DataFrame({
    "Bot": ["Bot A", "Bot B", "Bot C", "Bot D"],
    "Current Liability (£)": [250, 400, 300, 150],
    "Max Liability (£)": [500, 500, 500, 500],
    "Risk Status": ["Medium", "High", "Medium", "Low"]
}).set_index("Bot")

# Page Title
st.title("🚧 Risk & Liability Management")

# Liability Overview
st.subheader("Current Liability Overview")
st.bar_chart(risk_liability_data["Current Liability (£)"])

# Risk Status
st.subheader("Risk Status by Bot")
st.dataframe(risk_liability_data[["Risk Status"]], use_container_width=True)

# Detailed Risk Insights
for bot, row in risk_liability_data.iterrows():
    with st.expander(f"Details for {bot}"):
        st.write(f"Current Liability (£): {row['Current Liability (£)']}")
        st.write(f"Max Liability (£): {row['Max Liability (£)']}")
        st.write(f"Risk Status: {row['Risk Status']}")
```

